Z||000000||Nikotek||05-09-2001||11:01 AM||||Thanks for taking the time and quite a forum here,the most knowledgable group I've ever seen. I've had an 88' coupe 4cyl since new,unfortunately I let it sit for 3 years.Electrical seems good:new plugs,wires,fuel,oil ect.I hear the click for the relay behind my head but no fuel pump sounds(also verified no spray from the injector).I'm wondering if anyone has any tips on testing various obscure electrical or other systems possibly inline with the system.I can't imagine the pump going bad it was replaced 2,000 miles before it was parked,and my oil preesure sending unit rattles and isn't stuck.Thanks again for the help and looking forward to helping everyone else with my 2cents-I'll try to post pics of my 355 kit for anyone interested!<P>------------------<BR>87' GT (355 Spyder)<BR>88' Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-09-2001||11:31 AM||||First, Welcome to the Forum. Was the gas tank full of gas when you parked it? It could be varnished up. I would check the fuel pump fuse and also see if you have pressure in the fuel line. The injector could be frozen closed also. You may need to drop the pump to clean it if it is heavily varnished.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nikotek||05-09-2001||11:39 AM||||Thanks for the reply,I believe it had around 1/4 tank...I have noticed that even though the entire throttle body and injector was replaced a few years back,the injector has a light orang look to it on the screens-might be rust.<P>------------------<BR>87' GT (355 Spyder)<BR>88' Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-09-2001||12:11 PM||||If the tank was only 1/4 full then you most likely have a varnished fuel pump. Odds are the fuel tank float is varnished too so even if you fill the tank it may still be stuck at 1/4 tank. Best bet is to drop the tank and clean it out. Be careful with the float. It costs over $300 to replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nikotek||05-09-2001||12:19 PM||||Seems the last thing I want to do is drop the tank,but you may be right-I may not be able to avoid it.I think I'll throw in some Marvel Mystery Oil and see how good it is!Thanks for the help Oreif.<P>------------------<BR>87' GT (355 Spyder)<BR>88' Coupe||||reg||1
